<title>UK: Maiden pre-tax profits rise in half year.</title>
<headline>Maiden pre-tax profits rise in half year.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		7.7		    vs 5.6</p>
<p> Gross profit	     9.27		   vs 5.30</p>
<p> Pretax		     3.18		   vs 1.97</p>
<p>Turnover		   26.76		  vs 14.53</p>
<p> Operating profit	 4.08		   vs 2.57</p>
<p>NOTE - Maiden Group Plc, which floated on the stock exchange in May, said the first dividend proposed will be the final dividend for the year ending December 31, payable in May 1997.</p>
</text>
